1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,987
Nintendo Switch 2 Gets Replaceable Battery Version.

2
00:00:03,937 --> 00:00:15,200
Nintendo is introducing a replaceable battery version of the Switch 2 specifically for the European market, driven by upcoming EU battery regulations set to take effect in 2027.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:24,337
The new regulation requires all consumer electronics to feature user-replaceable batteries, forcing Nintendo to redesign its hardware for compliance.

4
00:00:24,337 --> 00:00:30,912
Meanwhile, the original Nintendo Switch will be discontinued across Europe starting in 2027.

5
00:00:30,912 --> 00:00:44,500
On the pricing front, the Switch 2 is set to rise from its current $450 launch price to $500 beginning September 2026, a move Nintendo attributes to increased component costs and inflation.

6
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:52,600
The replaceable battery model is expected to roll out across other regions over time, though no timeline has been confirmed outside Europe.

7
00:00:52,600 --> 00:01:03,125
The changes mark a significant hardware shift for Nintendo as it navigates evolving regulatory landscapes while maintaining its dominant position in the handheld and hybrid console market.

